{
  "comment": [
    "Every glyph in Resources/Fonts/IconFont.ttf; rebuild it, and Source/Utility/Icons.h, with",
    "Resources/Fonts/IconFont/build_icon_font.py. This is the only place icons are declared.",
    "An entry is the Icons:: names that select the glyph plus its single artwork source:",
    "fluent names an icon in Microsoft's Fluent System Icons, always the _24_ asset, which",
    "the builder reads from the pinned npm package; file names an SVG drawn for plugdata,",
    "on a 2048-unit square canvas with y pointing down from the typographic ascender",
    "(SVG y = 1638 - fontY), containing filled <path> contours with strokes expanded.",
    "There are no per-glyph transforms or advances: every canvas is scaled onto the em and",
    "every glyph is one em wide, so an icon's size is decided by its artwork alone.",
    "Codepoints are assigned in order from firstCodepoint and only exist in the font and in",
    "the generated header; a bare string starts a section, which becomes a header comment."
  ],
  "unitsPerEm": 2048,
  "ascender": 1638,
  "advance": 2048,
  "firstCodepoint": "U+E000",
